T476	Quotation 135021 135076	"Auntie, I wish I hadn't done it-- but I didn't think."
T477	Quotation 135077 135388	"Oh, child, you never think. You never think of anything but your own selfishness. You could think to come all the way over here from Jackson's Island in the night to laugh at our troubles, and you could think to fool me with a lie about a dream; but you couldn't ever think to pity us and save us from sorrow."
T478	Quotation 135389 135535	"Auntie, I know now it was mean, but I didn't mean to be mean. I didn't, honest. And besides, I didn't come over here to laugh at you that night."
T479	Quotation 135536 135566	"What did you come for, then?"
T480	Quotation 135567 135646	"It was to tell you not to be uneasy about us, because we hadn't got drownded."
T481	Quotation 135647 135813	"Tom, Tom, I would be the thankfullest soul in this world if I could believe you ever had as good a thought as that, but you know you never did-- and I know it, Tom."
T482	Quotation 135814 135886	"Indeed and 'deed I did, auntie -- I wish I may never stir if I didn't."
T483	Quotation 135887 135966	"Oh, Tom, don't lie-- don't do it. It only makes things a hundred times worse."
T484	Quotation 135967 136077	"It ain't a lie, auntie; it's the truth. I wanted to keep you from grieving-- that was all that made me come."
T485	Quotation 136078 136277	"I'd give the whole world to believe that-- it would cover up a power of sins, Tom. I'd 'most be glad you'd run off and acted so bad. But it ain't reasonable; because, why didn't you tell me, child?"
T486	Quotation 136278 136504	"Why, you see, when you got to talking about the funeral, I just got all full of the idea of our coming and hiding in the church, and I couldn't somehow bear to spoil it. So I just put the bark back in my pocket and kept mum."
T487	Quotation 136505 136517	"What bark?"
T488	Quotation 136518 136638	"The bark I had wrote on to tell you we'd gone pirating. I wish, now, you'd waked up when I kissed you -- I do, honest."
T489	Quotation 136725 136748	"DID you kiss me, Tom?"
T490	Quotation 136749 136767	"Why, yes, I did."
T491	Quotation 136768 136796	"Are you sure you did, Tom?"
T492	Quotation 136797 136838	"Why, yes, I did, auntie-- certain sure."
T493	Quotation 136839 136871	"What did you kiss me for, Tom?"
T494	Quotation 136872 136944	"Because I loved you so, and you laid there moaning and I was so sorry."
T495	Quotation 137040 137129	"Kiss me again, Tom!-- and be off with you to school, now, and don't bother me any more."
T496	Quotation 137299 137591	"No, I don't dare. Poor boy, I reckon he's lied about it-- but it's a blessed, blessed lie, there's such a comfort come from it. I hope the Lord -- I KNOW the Lord will forgive him, because it was such goodheartedness in him to tell it. But I don't want to find out it's a lie. I won't look."
T497	Quotation 138396 138540	"I acted mighty mean to-day, Becky, and I'm so sorry. I won't ever, ever do that way again, as long as ever I live-- please make up, won't you?"
T498	Quotation 138597 138693	"I'll thank you to keep yourself TO yourself, Mr. Thomas Sawyer. I'll never speak to you again."
T499	Quotation 141077 141258	"You ought to be ashamed of yourself, Tom Sawyer; you know you're going to tell on me, and oh, what shall I do, what shall I do! I'll be whipped, and I never was whipped in school."
T500	Quotation 140918 141028	"Tom Sawyer, you are just as mean as you can be, to sneak up on a person and look at what they're looking at."
T501	Quotation 141029 141076	"How could I know you was looking at anything?"
T502	Quotation 142347 142431	"All right, though; she'd like to see me in just such a fix-- let her sweat it out!"
T503	Quotation 141577 142292	"What a curious kind of a fool a girl is! Never been licked in school! Shucks! What's a licking! That's just like a girl-- they're so thin-skinned and chicken-hearted. Well, of course I ain't going to tell old Dobbins on this little fool, because there's other ways of getting even on her, that ain't so mean; but what of it? Old Dobbins will ask who it was tore his book. Nobody'll answer. Then he'll do just the way he always does-- ask first one and then t'other, and when he comes to the right girl he'll know it, without any telling. Girls' faces always tell on them. They ain't got any backbone. She'll get licked. Well, it's a kind of a tight place for Becky Thatcher, because there ain't any way out of it."
T504	Quotation 141302 141428	"BE so mean if you want to! I know something that's going to happen. You just wait and you'll see! Hateful, hateful, hateful!"
T505	Quotation 143539 143631	"he'll tell about me tearing the picture sure. I wouldn't say a word, not to save his life!"
T506	Quotation 145252 145273	"Who tore this book?"
T507	Quotation 145411 145453	"Benjamin Rogers, did you tear this book?"
T508	Quotation 145479 145504	"Joseph Harper, did you?"
T509	Quotation 145695 145710	"Amy Lawrence?"
T510	Quotation 145732 145748	"Gracie Miller?"
T511	Quotation 145764 145796	"Susan Harper, did you do this?"
T512	Quotation 145951 145969	"Rebecca Thatcher"
T513	Quotation 146025 146065	"did you tear-- no, look me in the face"
T514	Quotation 146095 146120	"did you tear this book?"
T515	Quotation 146208 146220	"I done it!"
T516	Quotation 147223 147256	"Tom, how COULD you be so noble!"
